\begin{equation*}
\bar{\mathfrak F}(\bar U)
=\varinjlim_i(\varphi_i^*\mathfrak F)(U_i).
\end{equation*}
On $(\varphi_i^*\mathfrak F)(U_i)$, the group
$\operatorname{Gal}(\bar k/k)$ acts through
$\operatorname{Gal}(k_i/k)$, which proves (i).

The functor in (ii) has as right adjoint the functor
\begin{equation*}
\mathfrak G\longmapsto
(\bar\varphi_*\mathfrak G)^{\operatorname{Gal}(\bar k/k)}.
\end{equation*}
For every $\mathfrak F$ on $Y$, one has
\begin{equation*}
\bar\varphi_*\bar\varphi^*\mathfrak F
=\varinjlim_i\varphi_{i*}\varphi_i^*\mathfrak F.
\end{equation*}
Thus, to prove that
\begin{equation*}
\mathfrak F\xrightarrow{\sim}
(\bar\varphi_*\bar\varphi^*\mathfrak F)^{
  \operatorname{Gal}(\bar k/k)},
\end{equation*}
it is enough to prove, for every $i$, that
\begin{equation*}
